attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a single spine column.** Column 0, `yhaJ`, is carried by 100% of chromosomes, persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0.2% of calls {S1}. The model names 99.8% of them, at 0.08 bits {S1}.

@variable **A variable column follows at `yhaI`**, column 1, carried by 80% {S2.c1}. Then columns 2 to 22, `yhaH` to `rlmG`, are a spine carried by 95 to 97%, [[hexuronate catabolism]] at columns 12 to 14 {S3, Q}. Through columns 58 to 62 a branch of 5 shell families runs in 10 to 11%, [[fimbrial biogenesis]] {S6.b58, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 96 against 89%, and hesitates less there, 0.18 against 0.41 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 61, a fork column, 0.85 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends in fork and variable columns.** Columns 41 to 79 are carried by 40 to 90%, in a region of plasticity in 11 to 49% of calls {S6, P}. The last column is `qseC`, in 42% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 92% of genes**, 0.30 bits on average, perplexity 1.5 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 1.48 against 0.15 bits, and names fewer genes, 67% against 96% {C}.

